[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2605265000-district-heating-cooling-d-gate-evaluation-r0", :adr/title "District heating + cooling networks — D1..D5 evaluation R0 (sub-ADR of 2605263500; cross-actor heat-network architecture from 2605264300 §5 elevated to substrate layer)", :adr/status "proposed-pending-council-ratification", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2605265000: District heating + cooling networks — D1..D5 evaluation R0\n\n**Status**: proposed-pending-council-ratification\n**Date**: 2026-05-26\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (Founder, Seat 1) — pending Council Lv7+ unanimity cascade\n\n# Context\n\nADR-2605264300 §5 (CSP/solar process heat) and ADR-2605264500 §4 (geothermal deep) both reference an implicit heat-network architecture connecting heat sources to heat consumers across actors. As religious-corp scale grows past R3, the heat network becomes a substrate primitive that deserves explicit constitutional treatment:\n\n- Per-consumer metering raises privacy concerns (hikari N7 inheritance)\n- Loss accounting + billing policy needs framework (not ad-hoc per facility)\n- District energy is a major commercial utility sector globally — explicit boundary needed\n\nDistrict-energy generations:\n\n| Gen | Working fluid | Temp | Era | Religious-corp fit |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **1G** | Steam | 200-300°C | 1880s-1930s | ✗ §2 |\n| **2G** | High-pressure hot water | 100-200°C | 1930s-1970s | ✗ §2 |\n| **3G** | Medium-pressure hot water | 80-120°C | 1970s-2010s | DEFERRED §2 |\n| **4G** (4GDH) | Low-temp water | 30-70°C | 2010s-present | ✓ §1 |\n| **5G** (5GDH/5DHC) | Ambient-temp loop (10-25°C) + per-building heat pump | ambient | R&D | ✓ §1 (preferred R&D scale) |\n\n# Decision\n\n## §1 4th + 5th generation district heat/cool — CONDITIONALLY PERMITTED\n\n≤2 MW thermal per network through R3; ≤5 networks religious-corp aggregate.\n\n| Gate | Assessment |\n|---|---|\n| **D1** | ✓ Religious-corp-owned network infrastructure; heat sources per upstream ADRs (CSP / geothermal / biomethane CHP / DAC waste-heat) all religious-corp |\n| **D2** | ✓ No long-lived waste; pipe insulation + jointing materials short-cycle; EOL recyclable per analog of hikari G7 |\n| **D3** | ✓ No combustion at network level; embodied-CO₂ of pipe + insulation amortized over 30+ yr lifetime |\n| **D4** | ✓ No fissile |\n| **D5** | ✓ Pipe + heat-exchanger + pump + SCADA controller open-hardware Apache 2.0 + Rider; network operator software open-source |\n\n**Conditions** (cross-actor framework):\n\n1. Per-network ≤2 MW thermal through R3 (proportionate scale; >2 MW = sub-utility scale Council Lv6+ ≥3 per network R3+; >10 MW = hikari N6 utility prohibition analog)\n2. **Religious-corp ownership exclusive**: pipe-in-ground + buildings-served + heat-source per network MUST all be religious-corp-attested per LANDS.md + `hikari.installAttestation`. Commercial district-energy utility (Veolia / E.ON / Vattenfall / Fortum / Engie / DECP partnership) participation **ABSOLUTELY PROHIBITED** (D1 commercial-utility-vendor + hikari G13 commercial-resale)\n3. **Per-consumer metering aggregate-only per hikari R0 N7 inheritance**: heat delivery per consumer building per ≥1-hour bucket; NO per-room / per-radiator / per-appliance telemetry; NO per-individual usage attribution\n4. **Billing policy = cost-recovery only**: per consumer share = (operating cost + amortized capex + reserves) × consumer's measured share / total network energy; NO profit margin (Charter §2(b) financialization-of-public-goods); rates Council-approved annually via `toritate.ledgerEntry`\n5. **Loss accounting MANDATORY**: network heat-loss audit annual; transmission losses <15% of source heat (4GDH typical 10-15%); aggregate-only reporting on IPFS (per network, not per pipe segment which would reveal route-and-consumer mapping)\n6. **mizuho cross-actor for water-based networks**: working-fluid water (4GDH closed-loop) registered per `mizuho.waterSupplySourceRegistry` + makeup water sourcing per mizuho R2+ infrastructure\n7. **Pipe material**: pre-insulated PEX (polyethylene cross-linked) or pre-insulated steel; lifetime expectation ≥30 yr (multi-gen invariant per §1.9); jointing per ISO 13760 / EN 253 equivalent open-publication\n8. **Pipe routing public-comment**: route map published on IPFS during commissioning planning + 30-day public-comment period (G10 of hikari analog — neighborhood transparency)\n9. **SCADA controller**: Murakumo-only inference for network optimization per ADR-2605215000; NO commercial DCS / SCADA vendor (Siemens / Honeywell / Yokogawa / Emerson proprietary) — open-source replacements (OpenSCADA / FUXA / Rapid SCADA) acceptable if Charter Rider §2 audit passes\n10. **5G-preferred where heat-source temperature permits**: 5GDH/5DHC ambient-loop allows bidirectional thermal sharing (one building's cooling waste = another's heating supply); per-building heat-pump architecture distributes the temperature-lift task and shrinks distribution losses. R&D-scale priority over 4GDH where new construction\n11. Annual `silenDistrictHeatReview` Council Lv6+ ≥3: per-network loss audit + billing transparency + privacy attestation (N7 compliance)\n\n## §2 1G + 2G + 3G high-temperature steam/water networks — DEFERRED or PROHIBITED\n\n| Gen | Verdict | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1G steam | PROHIBITED | High pressure (≥20 bar) + steam-trap losses + materials corrosion = unjustifiable for religious-corp scale; obsolete |\n| 2G high-pressure water (100-200°C) | PROHIBITED | Similar pressure + thermal-stress burden vs negligible benefit at religious-corp scale |\n| 3G medium-pressure water (80-120°C) | DEFERRED | Only consideration if existing 3G commercial network is acquired by religious-corp as part of LANDS parcel + 30-day Council retrofit-or-decommission ADR |\n\n## §3 District cooling — same framework as §1 with chilled-water-loop sibling\n\nSame conditions as §1 but distributing chilled water (4°C supply / 10°C return) instead of low-temp heating water. Heat-source for chilling = absorption chiller fed by §1 of CSP-thermal OR geothermal OR biomethane CHP waste heat (cross-actor 2605264300 §5); compression chiller fed by hikari electricity acceptable but absorption preferred for renewable-cycle integration.\n\n5DHC (ambient loop with per-building heat pump capable of both heating and cooling) is the unified preferred path.\n\n## §4 Cross-actor mesh\n\n| Actor | Role | Direction |\n|---|---|---|\n| **CSP / solar process heat** (ADR-2605264300) | Heat source 30-200°C | → network |\n| **Geothermal medium-depth** (ADR-2605264500) | Heat source 90-200°C | → network |\n| **Biomethane CHP** (ADR-2605263800 §1.7(a)) | Heat + electricity source | → network + grid |\n| **DAC regeneration heat** (ADR-2605264600) | Heat sink (consumer) OR co-generation source | ←→ network |\n| **Industrial process heat** (igata cement-curing 40-80°C; yakushi WFI preheat 80-100°C; biomethane digester 35-55°C) | Heat sink (consumer) | ← network |\n| **Facility heating** (iyashi / hagukumi / manabi / mitsuho greenhouse) | Heat sink (consumer) | ← network |\n| **mizuho** R2+ | Working-fluid water + makeup | ← network |\n| **toritate** R1+ | Billing accounting + transparency | (audit) |\n| **chigiri** R1+ | Consumer agreement + dispute mediation | (procedural) |\n\n## §5 Roadmap\n\n| Phase | Scope | Cap |\n|---|---|---|\n| **R0** | This ADR; path-reserved `orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-hikari/cells/district_heat_network/` + `district_cool_network/` import-time RuntimeError | None |\n| **R1** | post-Council + hikari R2 heat-source + mizuho R2 + ≥1 thermal-engineer on Council | Single ≤200 kW thermal 4GDH OR 5GDH/5DHC network serving ≤5 consumer buildings | 1 network |\n| **R2** | post-R1 + 30-day public + 1-yr safe operation + billing-transparency attestation | ≤500 kW thermal per network + 5G ambient-loop pilot | 3 networks |\n| **R3** | post-R2 + Council Lv6+ ≥3 + cross-actor toritate billing-audit cycle | Full §1 caps | 5 networks |\n\n## §6 New Lexicons (R1+)\n\n```\ncom.etzhayyim.hikari.{\n  districtHeatNetworkAttestation,         # network ID + LANDS pipe-route + heat source CIDs + ≤2 MW cap\n  districtCoolNetworkAttestation,         # same shape for chilled-water / ambient-loop\n  networkLossAuditRecord,                 # annual per-network loss % + transmission distance + average ΔT\n  networkBillingPolicy,                   # cost-recovery formula + Council rate-approval CID\n  consumerDeliveryRecord,                 # aggregate ≥1-hour bucket per consumer building (NOT per-room/appliance)\n  silenDistrictHeatReview                 # annual Council Lv6+ ≥3 across all networks\n}\n```\n\n# Consequences\n\n**Positive**:\n- Promotes ad-hoc heat-network into a substrate primitive with consistent privacy + billing + loss policy\n- 5GDH/5DHC ambient-loop unlocks bidirectional thermal sharing (district as buffer)\n- Cross-actor binding makes religious-corp facilities sub-MWh-rebatedeable without per-consumer overhead\n\n**Negative**:\n- Capex ~$2,000-5,000 per meter of pipe (≤2 MW network ~$2-10M total)\n- 30-yr lifetime burden requires multi-gen stewardship attestation\n- Commercial-utility vendor lock-out limits SCADA tooling choice (open-source SCADA maturity gap)\n- 5G ambient-loop requires per-building heat-pump installation (capex shift to consumer side)\n\n# References\n\n- ADR-2605263500 (parent D1..D5)\n- ADR-2605264300 §5 (heat-network architecture promoted to first-class here)\n- ADR-2605264500 §4 (heat-network sibling)\n- ADR-2605263100 (mizuho cross-actor for working-fluid water)\n- ADR-2605264900 (N7 + billing-transparency precedent)\n- ISO 13760 / EN 253 — pre-insulated pipe standards (referenced)\n- IEA DHC TCP — open-publication 4GDH / 5GDH reference\n- \"4th Generation District Heating (4GDH)\" Lund et al. *Energy* 68 (2014) — referenced concept reference\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2605265000-district-heating-cooling-d-gate-evaluation-r0.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "district-heating-cooling-d-gate-evaluation", :adr/last_verified "2026-05-26", :adr/date "2026-05-26", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/related ["adr-2605263800-biomethane-d-gate-evaluation-r0"], :adr/authoritative_for ["District heat/cool generations (1G-5G) D1..D5 evaluation" "Network ownership invariant (religious-corp + mizuho water-rights cross-actor; NO commercial utility)" "Per-consumer metering aggregate-only (≥1-hour buckets per hikari N7 inheritance)" "Loss-accounting + billing-policy framework (cost-recovery model only; NO profit-rate)"]}]
